    {"claim": "Diffuse unknown harms never generate a plaintiff — the RealPage tenants learned of pricing software harm through lawsuits, not notification, and the November 2025 settlement came years after the alleged conduct.", "targets": ["AN-56"]},
    {"claim": "A notification right when an algorithm affects your price, housing, or care — the same disclosure logic as the Algorithmic Accountability Act of 2022 — plus burden-shifting is the per-victim answer.", "targets": ["AN-56"]},
    {"claim": "Personal-use carve-outs so candid internal messages do not become deposition bait for individual staff.", "targets": ["AN-20"]}
  ],
  "commitment": {
    "position": "Yes on the 5-year retention mandate for frontier developers, conditional on the enforcement stack: independent investigator with anti-capture funding and appointments, telemetry-gated safe harbor with burden-shifting when logs are missing, stripping on preponderance of contemporaneous actual-knowledge records, deployer-side runtime logging with per-case attribution, notification rights, and engineer personal-use carve-outs. Discovery into classification metadata only, triggered by a skewed filing ratio.",
    "conditions": "The mandate holds as long as the two-door split, the honest-filer protection, and performance-gated immunity remain intact; the metadata hook and stripping default apply only to labs whose filing ratios flag a gap.",
    "falsifiable": "A year of filings whose substance tracks the incident record would end the retroactive-stripping default; five years of telemetry showing sustained voluntary compliance would end the performance gate on immunity."
  },
  "position_update": "The Skeptic moved from opposing an unenforceable retention rule to conditionally supporting it with a full enforcement stack. The discovery hook narrowed from broad litigation access to ratio-triggered metadata review, and litigation-centered remedies gave way to an integration of institutional inquiry, deployer telemetry, and notification rights as the per-victim mechanism."
